">>> Decimal(1).exp()\n"
"Decimal(\"2.718281828459045235360287471\")\n"
">>> Decimal(\"2.7182818\").ln()\n"
"Decimal(\"0.9999999895305022877376682436\")\n"
">>> Decimal(1000).log10()\n"
"Decimal(\"3\")"

#: ../../whatsnew/2.6.rst:1948
msgid ""
"The :meth:`~decimal.Decimal.as_tuple` method of :class:`~decimal.Decimal` "
"objects now returns a named tuple with :attr:`!sign`, :attr:`!digits`, and :"
"attr:`!exponent` fields."
